    "turn_text": "by unelected judges that should never have occurred. And the court last week rightly made the decision that this really isn't a right under the Constitution, and it needs to be left up to the people, the elected representatives of the people, and they gave the power back, which that is, you know, so unusual and historic that a one of the three branches of government says, hey, we've got too much power, we're going to give it back. Right. Yeah but the bottom line is that more lives are going to be safe now and there are many many states that have already passed laws including here in Missouri that we are a pro-life state and there will not be abortion here unless the life of the mother is in jeopardy and we are embracing the mother in this process there are multiple pregnancy care centers throughout our state and standing ready to support every woman in an unplanned pregnancy situation, giving her the support to make sure that that baby is brought to life and helping her in her parenting or if she wants to make a parenting decision and for her child through adoption. There are other ways to handle these situations and I'm excited for the lives that are going to get to live. We've lost 63 million Americans at the hands of abortion since 1973. And my heart just breaks for wondering what, you know, what plan God had for each one of those children. Who knows, you know, we maybe have had a cure for Alzheimer's or cancer by now. We don't know what contributions they could have given to us. And so now more babies will be able to live and it'll be good for all of us.",
