    "turn_text": "Well, you're right. And I think what we've seen, you know, if you really take the notion that it's not a life, if you say it's not a life, there's a callousness that builds both in men and women. And like I said, I've seen your leadership, we're trying to reinstil life, reinstil the sanctity of all life. Men take their responsibility seriously, women take their responsibility seriously. How do we start to reinstil this? So the Supreme Court said, okay, it's not constitutional. But now, we've had a culture that actually had a veneer of respectability over abortion for over 50 years. That veneer is gone, but now the real debate begins. So how do we reinstate that? I know your job as a congresswoman is not, I mean, it's our job at the church, the family, that as well. But how do we rein still going forward from your perspective?",
